{"kind":"table","sheet":"Template","address":"A1:E37","rows":37,"cols":5,"values":[["It is recommended that you do not edit rubrics in spreadsheet format",null,null,null,null],["v1.0-s",null,null,null,null],["Name, class, and date",null,null,null,null],["Enter your complete name, class, and date in the final presentation.",null,null,null,null],[null,1,0,null,null],[null,"Complete","Incomplete",null,null],[null,"1 pt = complete name, class, and date.","0 pts = name, class, or date is missing or incomplete.",null,null],["Four-slide structure, title, topic, and question",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: (1) uses the teacher-provided presentation template; (2) includes at least four slides; (3) Slide 1 has a clear title, the student's full name, and the selected topic; and (4) Slide 1 includes one clear main question related to the topic.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or no presentation."],["Topic explanation and importance",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: Slide 2 (1) clearly explains the selected data topic; (2) uses accurate information; (3) explains why the topic is important in modern society; and (4) connects the explanation to careful or responsible handling of data.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or no explanation."],["Real-life example and evidence",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: Slide 3 (1) includes one clear real-life example related to the selected topic; and includes (2) a first, (3) a second, and (4) a third accurate evidence statement that supports or explains the example.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or no example/evidence."],["Risk and recommendations",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: Slide 4 (1) identifies one realistic risk related to the selected topic; and gives (2) a first, (3) a second, and (4) a third practical recommendation for handling data more carefully or responsibly.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or no risk/recommendations."],["Conclusion, visuals, readability, and English",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: (1) Slide 4 includes a clear final conclusion that answers or responds to the main question; (2) uses short, understandable sentences; (3) includes clear and relevant images or icons and readable text; and (4) all required presentation content is written in clear English.",null,null,null,null],[null,7,5,3,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"7 pts = 4 checks.","5 pts = 2–3.","3 pts = 1.","0 pts = 0 or presentation is not readable."],["Punctuality, readiness, and respect",null,null,null,null],["4 checks: (1) Submits all required work by the deadline; (2) arrives with a charged computer, charger, login access, pen, and notebook; (3) handles the computer, charger, and workspace carefully; and (4) begins on time, follows directions, and does not interfere with another student’s device or work.",null,null,null,null],[null,4,3,1,0],[null,"Meets Standard","Approaches Standard","Below Standard","Unacceptable"],[null,"4 pts = 4 steps.","3 pts = 2–3.","1 pt = 1.","0 pts = none."]]}
